// C11 6.9p3 / 6.9.2: at most one initialized definition of a file-scope
// object per TU. `int x = 1; int x = 2;` reached MIR as two definitions and
// died there — "MIR fatal error: Repeated item declaration x", no source
// location, process exit (the host-killing path in an eval / REPL / parse
// handle). Now a located front-end diagnostic (Program::declare_object).
// Oracle: gcc and clang "redefinition of 'x'" (g++ / clang++ likewise).
#include <stdio.h>
int x = 1;
int x = 2;
int main(void)
{
	printf("%d\n", x);
	return 0;
}
